            "normalized_html": "<p>We are given the equation <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 7(2q - 3) = 5(2q - 3) + 18]</span> and are asked to find the value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2q - 3.]</span></p><p>We begin by combining like terms:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 7(2q \u2212 3)|= 5(2q \u2212 3) + 18; 7(2q \u2212 3) \u2212 5(2q \u2212 3)|= 18; (7 \u2212 5)(2q \u2212 3)|= 18; 2(2q \u2212 3)|= 18]</span></p><p>Next, we divide both sides by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2]</span> to isolate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2q - 3{:}]</span>\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2q \u2212 3|= 9]</span></p><p>So, the value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2q - 3]</span> is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9.]</span></p>",
